$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The lactol (6.48 g, 54.8 mmol) was dissolved in toluene (300 mL) to which
was added methyl 2-(triphenylphosphoranylidene)propanoate (38.2 g, 109.7
mmol). The mixture was placed in an oil bath at 90 °C for 3 h under Ar.
When the reaction was complete, as monitored by TLC, the solvent was
evaporated in vacuo to give a yellow oil, which was then purifi ed by
flash column chromatography (SiO2, 30% EtOAc/hexane) to provide
(4S,2E)-methyl 6-hydroxy-4-methoxy-2-methylhex-2-enoate 17 in almost
quantitative yield (∼10.2 g, 99%), with selectivity of E/Z = 10/1. The
pure E isomer could not be obtained readily at this point by silica gel
chromatography. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C) δ = 6.65 (d, J = 9.3 Hz, 1
H), 4.15-4.32 (m, 2 H), 3.78 (m, 1 H), 3.77 (s, 3 H), 3.27 (s, 3 H), 2.50
(s, 1H, br, OH), 1.87 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 3 H), 1.80-1.90 (m, 1 H), 1.65-1.75
(m, 1 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 10:1 E:Z, E isomer not separable, Wittig reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total Synthesis of Iejimalide B
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Qingshou; Schweitzer, Dirk; Kane, John; Davisson, V. Jo; Helquist,
Paul
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2011), 76(13), 5157-5169

