$DATUM Olefin S39. To a suspension of Ph3P+CH3Br- (25.9 mg, 0.0725 mmol) in THF
(0.5 mL) at 0 °C was added NaHMDS (1.0 M solution in THF, 0.070 mL, 0.070
mmol), and the resultant suspension was stirred at 0 °C for 30 min. To
the suspension at -78 °C was added a solution of ketone S38 (17.4 mg,
0.0107 mmol) in THF (0.5 mL + 2 × 0.2 mL rinse), and the reaction mixture
was allowed to warm to 0 °C over 3 h. The reaction mixture was diluted
with saturated NH4Cl solution and extracted with EtOAc. The organic layer
was washed with H2O and brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by flash
column chromatography (silica gel, 35% EtOAc/hexanes) to give olefin S39.
Colorless oil, yield 16.8 mg, 97%. [α]D 21 -6.0 (c 1.00, CH2Cl2); IR
(film) 3053, 2952, 2871, 1726, 1458, 1380, 1341, 1164, 1123, 1081, 1040,
854, 815, 738 cm-1; 1H NMR (600 MHz, C6D6) δ 8.04 (m, 1H), 7.80-7.57 (m,
16H), 7.50 (m, 1H), 7.46 (m, 1H), 7.43 (m, 1H), 7.31-7.21 (m, 8H), 6.10
(ddd, J = 10.5, 10.5, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 5.63 (dd, J = 10.5, 10.5 Hz, 1H), 5.22
(d, J = 12.4 Hz, 1H), 5.04 (d, J = 12.4 Hz, 1H), 4.75 (d, J = 11.9 Hz,
1H), 4.69-4.64 (m, 3H), 4.56-4.43 (m, 4H), 4.36-4.29 (m, 2H), 4.26 (m,
1H), 4.12-4.02 (m, 3H), 3.69-3.61 (m, 3H), 3.56-3.31 (m, 8H), 3.30-3.10
(m, 6H), 2.96 (m, 1H), 2.91 (dd, J = 11.9, 3.2 Hz, 1H), 2.51 (dd, J =
12.8, 4.1 Hz, 1H), 2.41-2.32 (m, 2H), 2.27 (dd, J = 11.5, 3.2 Hz, 1H),
2.23-2.09 (m, 5H), 2.08-1.63 (m, 18H), 1.61-1.45 (m, 4H), 1.31 (s, 3H),
1.28 (s, 3H), 1.23 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 1.22 (s, 3H), 1.21 (d, J = 5.9
Hz, 3H), 1.18 (s, 9H), 1.08 (s, 3H), 0.87 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR
