$DATUM Ester S12: To a solution of aldehyde 17 (3.92g, 14.8 mmol) in benzene (50
mL) was added ylide 18 (6.45 g, 17.8 mmol). The solution was refluxed
overnight and after cooling to rt the reaction mixture was loaded
directly onto a column and purified (10% EtOAc/hexanes). 5.00 g of enoate
S12 (14.3 mmol, 97%) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm
7.24 (s, 2 H) 6.87 (d, J=8.48 Hz, 2 H) 6.53 (d, J=10.11Hz, 1H) 4.42 (s, 2
H) 4.18 (q, J=7.17 Hz, 2 H) 3.79 (s, 3 H) 3.41 (t, J=6.52 Hz, 2 H) 2.47
(m, 1H) 1.83 (s, 3 H) 1.58 (dddd, J=7.05, 7.05, 6.93, 6.68 Hz, 2 H) 1.32
(m, 9 H) 0.98 (d, J=6.85 Hz, 3 H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 168.29,
158.92, 147.86, 130.57, 129.04, 126.17, 113.55, 72.34, 69.88, 60.24,
55.06, 36.67, 33.05, 29.56, 27.17, 26.17, 19.90, 14.16, 12.40; IR (film):
2931, 2856, 1710, 1649, 1613, 1586, 1513, 1463, 1389, 1365, 1301, 1248,
1174, 1136, 1098, 1037; [α]25 D = −21 (c = 1.1, CH2Cl2); MS (ESI)
calculated for C21H32O4 M+ : 348.23, found 348.2379.
