$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 14: The aldehyde 13 (2.84 g, 11.46 mmol) was dissolved in
benzene (57 mL) and ethyl(triphenylphosphoranylidine)acetate (4.4 g, 12.6
mmol) was added. The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for
8 h when TLC examination revealed complete conversion of starting
material. The solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure, diethyl
ether (80 mL) was added to the residue and the reaction ure cooled to 0
°C. The precipitated solids were filtered and the filtrate was evaporated
to dryness. The residue thus obtained was purified by column
chromatography using 3% EtOAc/hexane (v/v) as the eluent to afford the
ester 14 (3.35 g, 10.54 mmol) in 92% yield as a viscous oil. TLC: Rf 0.5
(10% EtOAc/hexane). IR (neat): 3433, 2929, 2855, 1720, 1653, 1456, 1365,
1266, 1181, 1100, 1042, 736, 698 cm- 1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ
7.32-7.19 (m, 5H), 6.95-6.85 (m, 1H), 5.75 (d, J = 15.8 Hz, 1H), 4.46 (s,
2H), 4.15 (q, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 3.41 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 2.18 (q, J = 8.3
Hz, 2H), 1.62-1.53 (m, 2H), 1.52-1.40 (m, 2H), 1.39-1.26 (m, 11H). 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 166.4, 149.1, 138.5, 128.1, 127.4, 127.2, 121.1,
72.6, 70.2, 59.8, 31.9, 29.5, 29.1, 28.8, 27.8, 26.0, 14.1. MS (LC-MSD):
319 [M+H]+. HRMS (ESI): m/z [M+Na]+ calcd for C20H30O3Na 341.2092, found
341.2082.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
