$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for difluoromethylenation of
carbonyl compounds with reagent 3 (Table 1, entries 1-7, 9-12, 14-16):
Under N2 atmosphere, t-BuOK (100 mg, 0.89 mmol, 1.8 equiv) dissolved in
DMF (1mL) was added to a solution of 4-methoxybenzaldehyde (7a) (82 mg,
0.6 mmol, 1.2 equiv) and 2-(Difluoromethylsulfonyl)pyridine 3 (96mg, 0.5
mmol, 1.0 equiv) in 2 mL DMF at -50 oC (for entries 12 and 14, the
reaction was carried out on 0.3 mmol and 1.5 mL THF was added as a
cosolvent). The reaction mixture was allowed to warm up to -40 oC in
about 15 min (for entries 12 and 14, the reaction mixture was allowed to
warm up to -20 oC in about 3h). Then, the reaction is quenched with
aqueous saturated ammonium chloride (1mL), followed by 3N HCl (1mL). The
reaction mixture was allowed to warm up to rt (for aldehydes with
electron-withdrawing group, the reaction mixture was heated to 60 oC for
30 min), the completion of the reaction was monitored by 19F NMR. After
extraction with Et2O, the organic phase was successively washed with
brine, and then dried over anhydrous MgSO4. After the solution was
filtered and the solvent was evaporated under vacuum, the residue was
subjected to silica gel column chromatography to give product 8a (73 mg,
0.43 mmol, yield: 86%) as a colorless oil.
2-(2,2-Difluorovinyl)naphthalene (8g). White solid, yield 92% 1H NMR: δ
7.70-7.79 (m , 3H), 7.68 (s, 1H), 7.36-7.47 (m, 3H), 5.36 (dd, J = 25.8
Hz, J = 3.6 Hz 1H). 19F NMR: δ -82.62 (dd, J = 30.7 Hz, J = 26.2 Hz, 1F),
-84.30 (dd, J = 31.0 Hz, J = 3.9 Hz, 1F). MS (EI, m/z): 190 (M+, 100.0),
170 (25.1), 139 (20.1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Difluoromethyl 2-Pyridyl Sulfone: A New gem-Difluoroolefination Reagent
for Aldehydes and Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhao, Yanchuan; Huang, Weizhou; Zhu, Lingui; Hu, Jinbo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(7), 1444-1447

