$DATUM Ethyl des-A,B-25-(Ethoxymethyloxy)cholestan-8-ethylidencarboxylate (17).
To a suspension of NaH (366 mg, 60% oil suspension, 14.16 mmol) in
anhydrous THF (2.4 mL) at 0 ºC was added (EtO)2P(O)CH2CO2Et (3.3 mL,
16.52 mmol) and the mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight. A
solution of ketone 16 (400 mg, 1.18 mmol) in anhydrous THF (2.4 mL) was
added to the mixture at 0 ºC, and the reaction is stirred at the same
temperature for 72 h. Next, the reaction was poured into a saturated
aqueous solution of NH4Cl and extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic
fractions were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated. Purification of
the crude by column chromatography (5% EtOAc/hexane) gave 17 (ratio Z/E=
8:92) as a colorless oil in 92% yield. IR (NaCl): υ 2989, 2947, 2872,
1715 and 1645 cm-1; 1H NMR (300.13 MHz, CDCl3): major isomer (E) δ 0.58
(s, 3H), 0.94 (d, 3H, JHH 5.7 Hz), 1.16 (m, 1H), 1.22 (m, 9H), 1.25-2.1
(m, 20H), 3.61 (q, 2H, JHH 6.9 Hz), 3.85 (m, 1H), 4.15(q, 2H, JHH 6.9
Hz), 4.76 (s, 2H) and 5.46 (s, 1H) ppm; selected signals of minor isomer
(Z): 0.89 (d, 3H, Me, 3JHH 5.7 Hz) y 5.65 (s, 1H) ppm; 13C NMR (75.5 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 12.1 (CH3), 14.3 (CH3), 15.2 (CH3), 18.7 (CH3), 20.5 (CH2),
22.1 (CH2), 23.8 (CH2), 26.3 (CH3), 26.4 (CH3), 27.4 (CH2), 29.6 (CH),
36.0 (CH), 36.3 (CH2), 40.1 (CH2), 42.2 (CH2), 47.1 (C), 56.7 (CH), 56.8
(CH), 59.4 (CH2), 62.9 (CH2), 76.1 (C), 89.5 (CH2), 111.9 (CH), 163.3 (C)
and 166.9 (C) ppm; MS (ESI+, m/z): 431 [(M+Na)+, 100%].
