$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6,6-Ethylenedioxy-24-methyl-3α,5-cyclo-5α-cholest-22-ene (XVI). A
solution containing 0.88 g (3.9 mmol) of sulfone (V) in 35 ml of THF
cooled to -76°C was supplemented in an argon flow with 4.5 ml of a 1.2-N
butyllithium solution in hexane. The mixture was stirred at the same
temperature for 30 min and supplemented with 1.21 g (3.25 mmol) of
aldehyde (XII) in 15 ml of THF. Stirring of the mixture was continued at
a temperature of -76°C. After 2 h, the mixture was supplemented with 0.9
ml of acetic anhydride; the cooling bath was removed, and the reaction
mixture was left overnight. A saturated NH4Cl solution (20 ml) was added,
and the aqueous phase was separated from the organic phase to extract it
with petroleum ether (3 × 30 ml). The pooled organic phases were dried
with Na2SO4 and evaporated. The residue was dissolved in 250 ml of
absolute methanol, cooled to 0°C, and supplemented with 2.5 g of
activated magnesium and 1.0 g of HgCl2 under stirring. The reaction
mixture was stirred for 6 h and filtered through the layer of silica gel.
The filtrate was acidified with diluted acetic acid to pH 6 and extracted
with petroleum ether (3 × 30 ml). The extract was dried with Na2SO4 and
evaporated in a vacuum; the residue was separated by chromatography on a
silica gel column using a mixture of petroleum ether and ethyl acetate
(10 : 1) as an eluent. Totally, 0.64 g of compound (XVI) as an oil) and
0.62 g of initial aldehyde (XII) were obtained (the yield calculated per
reacted aldehyde (XII) was 91%). (Rf 0.28 (a). 1H NMR spectrum: 0.74 (3
H, s, H18), 0.79 (3 H, d, J 6.8, H21 or H24), 1.01 (3 H, s, H18), 1.08 (3
H, d, J 6.8, H24 or H21), 3.70-4.03 (4 H, m, dioxolane). 13C NMR
spectrum: 7.36, 12.43, 15.99, 16.34, 18.97, 22.61, 23.08, 24.48, 24.95,
27.71, 33.35, 34.19, 39.35, 40.09, 40.29, 43.03, 45.69, 46.58, 47.56,
49.80, 52.03, 55.75, 64.68, 64.92, 109.86, 214.10.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, key step, reactant also recovered, Julia olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of secasterol and 24-epi-secasterol and their toxicity for
MCF-7 cells
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
