$DATUM SYNTHESIS OF ALKENE 8. To a solution of sulfone (R)-7 (74.1 mg, 0.209
mmol) in THF (2 mL) at -78 °C was dropwise added NaHMDS (1.0 M in THF,
0.209 mL, 0.209 mmol). After the reaction mixture was stirred for 30 min,
a solution of 6 (49.0 mg, 0.0892 mmol) in THF (1.5 mL) was dropwise
added, and additional THF (0.5 mL) was used to rinse the vial containing
6, which was also added to the reaction solution. After the reaction was
stirred for 3 h at -78 °C, the reaction mixture was allowed to warm to rt
overnight. Then sat aq NaCl was added to quench the reaction, and the
solution was diluted by EtOAc (6 mL) and H2O (6 mL). The organic layer
was separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (2 × 15
mL). The combined organic layers were washed with sat aq NaCl, dried over
Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced pressure. Purification of the
crude residue via silica gel flash column chromatography (gradient
eluent: 10- 30% of EtOAc/hexanes) afforded the desired alkene 8 (54.4 mg,
90%) as a colorless oil. Alkene 8: Rf = 0.55 [20% EtOAc/Hexanes]; [α]D 23
= + 9.13 (c 0.23, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.48-0.60 (brm, 1H),
0.60-0.80 (brm, 1H), 0.92 (t, 3H, J = 7.0 Hz), 1.00-1.12 (m, 10H),
1.15-1.30 (brm, 5H), 1.30-1.53 (m, 17H), 1.60-1.90 (brm, 3H), 2.16-2.26
(brm, 3H), 3.38 (s, 3H), 3.48-3.62 (m, 1.5H), 3.70-3.82 (m, 0.5H), 4.13
(brs, 1H), 4.64 (d, 1H, J = 6.5 Hz), 4.69 (d, 1H, J = 7.0 Hz), 5.32-5.46
(m, 2H), 7.35-7.47 (m, 6H), 7.68 (q, 4H, J = 6.5 Hz); 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 14.3, 18.8, 19.3, 24.4, 24.8, 26.0, 27.1, 28.6, 30.3, 36.4,
36.6, 37.8, 40.5, 55.6, 68.0, 77.1, 79.0, 95.5, 127.5, 127.73, 127.78,
129.9, 131.3, 135.8, 135.9; IR (neat) cm-1 2931M, 2858m, 1687s, 1465m;
mass spectrum (APCI): m/e (% relative intensity) 578.4 (60) (M+H-Boc)+,
546.3 (100); HRMS (ESI): m/e calcd for C41H64NO5Si+ 678.4549, found
678.4536.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, last stage quench
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
