$DATUM Olefin 12. To a solution of alcohol S3 (1.75 g, 4.44 mmol) in CH2Cl2/DMSO
(1:1, v/v, 20 mL) at 0 °C were added Et3N (3.10 mL, 22.0 mmol) and
SO3·pyridine (2.83 g, 17.8 mmol), and the resultant mixture was stirred
at 0 °C for 1 h. The reaction mixture was diluted with Et2O and washed
successively with 1 M aqueous HCl solution, saturated aqueous NaHCO3
solution, and brine. The organic layer was dried over MgSO4, filtered,
and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residual crude aldehyde was
used in the next reaction without further purification. To a suspension
of Ph3P+CH3Br- (2.54 g, 7.11 mmol) in THF (30 mL) at 0 °C was added
t-BuOK (0.70 g, 6.24 mmol), and the resultant suspension was stirred at 0
°C for 30 min. To the resultant suspension at -78 °C was added a solution
of the above aldehyde in THF (5 mL + 2 × 2.5 mL rinse), and the resultant
mixture was allowed to warm to 0 °C and stirred at 0 °C for 2 h. The
reaction mixture was diluted with saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution and
extracted with EtOAc. The organic layer was washed with H2O and brine,
dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The
residue was purified by column chromatography (silica gel, 15%
EtOAc/hexanes) to give olefin 12 for the two steps. Colorless oil, yield
1.56 g, 90%. [α]D 18 +5.7 (c 1.00, CH2Cl2); IR (film) 2952, 2929, 2856,
1254, 1130, 1052, 1031, 835, 775 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.49-7.46 (m, 2H), 7.37-7.29 (m, 3H), 5.75 (ddd, J = 16.5, 10.0, 5.5 Hz,
1H), 5.44 (s, 1H), 5.27 (ddd, J = 16.5, 1.5, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.11 (ddd, J =
10.0, 1.5, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 4.24 (dd, J = 10.5, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 4.08 (m, 1H),
3.92 (m, 1H), 3.76 (ddd, J = 10.0, 10.0, 5.5 Hz, 1H), 3.58-3.50 (m, 2H),
2.10 (m, 1H), 1.87 (ddd, J = 5.5, 5.5, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 1.80-1.69 (m, 2H),
0.91 (s, 9H), 0.05 (s, 3H), 0.04 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ
138.0, 137.0, 128.9, 128.3 (2C), 126.2 (2C), 115.5, 100.9, 86.7, 81.8,
74.6, 71.8, 69.9, 25.9, 25.84 (3C), 25.81, 18.0, -4.3, -4.7; HRMS (ESI)
calcd for C22H34O4SiNa [(M + Na)+] 413.2119, found 413.2135.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM intermediates from stages 1 and 2 combined in stage 3, 74% overall yield
for 4 steps
