$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM C1-C38 fragment 2: To a flame-dried 5 mL round bottom flask in the dark
was added sulfone 34 (0.008 g, 0.012 mmol) and 0.12 mL DME. The solution
was cooled to −78 °C, at which time KHMDS (0.5 M in toluene, 24 µL, 0.012
mmol) was added dropwise via syringe. After stirring for 15 minutes,
aldehyde 31 (0.004 g, 0.006 mmol) in 0.12 mL DME was added dropwise via
syringe to the yellow solution. The reaction mixture was warmed to room
temperature over 2 hours then diluted with ether and quenched with sat.
NH4Cl. The aqueous layer was extracted 3x with diethyl ether, dried over
Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude
product was purified via flash column chromatography (5-30% EA/Hex,
silica gel pretreated with 0.5% Et3N). C1-C38 fragment 2 (0.0053 g, 79%)
as a light yellow oil, along with 2.4 mg of sulfone 34 (58%). 1H NMR (600
MHz, C6D6) δ 0.08 (s, 3H), 0.11 (s, 3H), 0.81 (d, J= 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.82
(d, J= 7.2 Hz, 3H), 0.99 (s, 9H), 1.04 (d, J= 6.4 Hz, 3H), 1.06-1.10 (m,
1H), 1.23-1.31 (m, 4H), 1.33 (s, 3H), 1.41 (s, 9H), 1.43-1.51 (m, 2H),
1.53 (s, 3H), 1.61-1.69 (m, 3H), 1.69-1.76 (m, 1H), 1.83 (s, 3H),
1.99-2.06 (m, 2H), 2.14-2.27 (m, 7H), 2.30-2.37 (m, 1H), 2.39-2.45 (m,
2H), 3.20 (s, 3H), 3.65-3.69 (m, 1H), 3.83-3.86 (m, 1H), 3.89 (br. s.,
1H), 3.92 (d, J= 6.0 Hz, 1H), 3.98 (ddd, J= 7.9, 7.9, 1.9 Hz, 1H), 4.01
(dd, J= 8.7, 7.9 Hz, 1H), 4.04-4.09 (m, 3H), 4.11 (br. s., 1H), 4.27 (t,
J= 7.2 Hz, 1H), 4.52-4.55 (m, 2H), 4.79 (t, J= 5.5 Hz, 1H), 5.45 (dd, J=
15.4, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 5.49-5.59 (m, 3H), 5.70 (ddd, J= 14.6, 7.2, 7.2 Hz,
1H), 5.75 (dd, J= 10.4, 2.5 Hz, 1H), 5.82 (dd, J= 14.7, 6.4 Hz, 1H), 5.87
(ddd, J= 10.2, 4.7, 2.1 Hz, 1H), 5.92-5.99 (m, 1H), 6.45 (dd, J= 14.7,
1.5 Hz, 1H), 6.83 (dd, J= 14.5, 4.7 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, C6D6): δ
172.5, 142.0, 133.1, 132.6, 132.5, 132.4, 132.1, 131.2, 129.5, 127.6,
127.0, 108.4, 95.1, 83.6, 80.6, 79.4, 79.3, 79.1, 79.0, 78.5, 76.7, 75.8,
75.5, 74.0, 72.7, 71.9, 66.0, 55.2, 41.8, 38.8, 37.8, 36.9, 36.4, 35.79,
35.76, 33.0, 32.9, 32.2, 29.6, 28.2, 27.5, 26.2, 25.74, 25.68, 21.3,
18.4, 15.2, 14.5, 10.8, −3.7, −4.2; IR (film): 2928, 2857, 1729, 1461,
1367, 1100, 1067, 1038, 837, 775; ESI-MS: C57H93INaO11Si [M+Na]+ calc.
1131.54, found 1131.50; [α]24 D = +45.0° (c = 0.27, C6H6).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative preparation shown, Julia-Kocienski
olefination, dropwise addition of KHMDS/toluene (stage 1), dropwise
addition of aldehyde/DME (stage 2), 55% of sulfone recovered
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Formal Synthesis of (+)-Sorangicin A
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Crimmins, Michael T.; Haley, Matthew W.; O'Bryan, Elizabeth A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
