$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Alkene 16 To a solution of sulfone 14 (5.83 g, 14.1 mmol) in DME (40 mL)
at -78 °C was added NaHMDS (24.7 mL, 14.8 mmol, 0.6 M in toluene). After
5 min, a solution of aldehyde 13 (4.05 g, 11.7 mmol) in DME (10 mL) was
added drop-wise via cannula. The reaction mixture was allowed to warm to
-50 °C. After 1 h, saturated aqueous NH4Cl (30 mL) was added, and the
reaction mixture was warmed to RT. The organics were extracted with EtOAc
(3 × 30 mL) and the combined organic extracts were washed with brine (100
mL), dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Hexane (30 mL)
was added, the solution was cooled (0 °C) and a white precipitate formed.
The mixture was filtered, washed with cold hexane and the crude was
concentrated in vacuo. This procedure was repeated until no more
precipitate formed. Purification by flash column chromatography (1%
EtOAc/Hexanes) provided alkene 16 (5.41 g, 86%) as a colourless oil.
Alkene 16, yield (5.41 g, 86%) Rf0.4 (10% EtOAc/Hexanes); [α]D20 -21.4 (c
3.1, CHCl3); IR (neat) 3029, 2930, 2857, 1254, 1115, 835, 776 cm-1; 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.36-7.21 (4H, m, Ar-H), 7.31-7.26 (1H, m, Ar-H),
5.42-5.37 (2H, m, H15 + H16), 4.50 (2H, s, PhCH2), 3.73-3.60 (1H, m,
H19), 3.56-3.36 (4H, m, H20 + H9), 2.24-1.91 (4H, m, H17 + H14),
1.69-1.52 (4H, m, H18 + H10), 1.40-1.27 (6H, m, H13 + H12 + H11), 0.89
(9H, s, SiC(CH3)3), 0.88 (9H, s, SiC(CH3)3), 0.05 (6H, s, 2 x SiCH3),
0.05 (3H, s, SiCH3), 0.04 (3H, s, SiCH3); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
138.6, 130.3, 130.1, 128.3, 127.6, 127.6, 127.4, 72.8, 72.6, 70.4, 67.3,
34.3, 32.5, 29.7, 29.5, 28.9, 28.2, 26.0, 25.9, 18.3, 18.1, -4.2, -4.7,
-5.3, -5.3; m/z (CI+) 557 (100, [M+Na]+); HRMS (CI+) Calc. for
C31H58O3Si2Na [M+Na]+ 557.3822, found 557.3816.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (E:Z = 97:3), dropwise addition of aldehyde stage 2
