$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical procedure for difluoromethylenation of carbonyl compounds with
reagent 3 (Table 1, entries 1-7, 9-12, 14-16): Under N2 atmosphere,
t-BuOK (100 mg, 0.89 mmol, 1.8 equiv) dissolved in DMF (1mL) was added to
a solution of 4-methoxybenzaldehyde (7a) (82 mg, 0.6 mmol, 1.2 equiv) and
2-(Difluoromethylsulfonyl)pyridine 3 (96mg, 0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in 2 mL
DMF at -50 oC (for entries 12 and 14, the reaction was carried out on 0.3
mmol and 1.5 mL THF was added as a cosolvent). The reaction mixture was
allowed to warm up to -40 oC in about 15 min (for entries 12 and 14, the
reaction mixture was allowed to warm up to -20 oC in about 3h). Then, the
reaction is quenched with aqueous saturated ammonium chloride (1mL),
followed by 3N HCl (1mL). The reaction mixture was allowed to warm up to
rt (for aldehydes with electron-withdrawing group, the reaction mixture
was heated to 60 oC for 30 min), the completion of the reaction was
monitored by 19F NMR. After extraction with Et2O, the organic phase was
successively washed with brine, and then dried over anhydrous MgSO4.
After the solution was filtered and the solvent was evaporated under
vacuum, the residue was subjected to silica gel column chromatography to
give product 8a (73 mg, 0.43 mmol, yield: 86%) as a colorless oil. 8a,
yield (73 mg, 0.43 mmol, 86%) 1H NMR: δ 7.16 (d, J = 8.2 Hz , 2H), 6.78
(d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 5.11 (dd, J = 26.7 Hz, J = 3.9 Hz, 1H), 3.70 (s,
3H). 19F NMR: δ -84.64 (dd, J = 37.5 Hz, J = 27.4 Hz, 1F), -86.44 (dd, J
= 36.9 Hz, J = 3.3 Hz, 1F). MS (EI, m/z): 170 (M+, 100.0), 155 (66.5),
127 (80.8) , 77 (18.5) , 51 (11.4).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Difluoromethyl 2-Pyridyl Sulfone: A New gem-Difluoroolefination Reagent
for Aldehydes and Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhao, Yanchuan; Huang, Weizhou; Zhu, Lingui; Hu, Jinbo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
