$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl (E)-octa-2,7-dienoate (S10). A well-stirred solution of oxalyl
chloride (90 mL, 180 mmol, 2 M in CH2Cl2) in anhydrous CH2Cl2 (300 mL) at
-78 °C was slowly treated with DMSO (21 mL, 300 mmol). After 15 min, a
solution of alcohol S9 (15 g, 150 mmol) in anhydrous CH2Cl2 was added to
the above mixture. The resulting suspension was allowed to stir at -78 °C
for 1 h and then treated with diisopropylethylamine (99 mL, 599 mmol).
The cooling bath was removed, and the reaction mixture was allowed to
stir at room temperature for 1 hr to afford a yellow solution of
aldehyde. The above solution was cooled again to 0 °C and treated with
methyl 2-(triphenylphosphoranylidene)acetate (60 g, 180 mmol). The
resulting reaction solution was allowed to stir at 0 °C for 1 h and
stirred at rt for overnight. Water (400 mL) and ether (700 mL) were
added. The two layers were separated and the organic layer was washed
with water (400 mL) and brine 350 mL. The organic phase was dried over
Na2SO4, concentrated and the yellow solids were mixed with 5% Et2O in
pentane (150 mL). The resulting mixture was filtered through a sintered
glass Buchner funnel and washed with 5% Et2O in pentane (50 mL). The
filtrate was concentrated and the residue was purified on silica column
(4% ether in pentane). 19.6 g (85%) of ester S10 as an oil. 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.00 - 6.92 (m, 1H), 5.86 - 5.71 (m, 2H), 5.06 - 4.92 (m,
2H), 3.72 (s, 3H), 2.24 - 2.18 (m, 2H), 2.12 - 2.02 (m, 2H), 1.56 (p, J =
7.4 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.1, 149.2, 137.9, 121.1,
115.1, 51.3, 33.0, 31.5, 27.1. The 1H NMR data matches the literature.7
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (stage 4), Swern oxidation (stage 1), Wittig-Horner
synthesis (stage 4)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pre-mRNA Splicing-Modulatory Pharmacophores: The Total Synthesis of
Herboxidiene, a Pladienolide-Herboxidiene Hybrid Analog and Related
Derivatives
