$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 39: Lithium hexamethyldisilazide (1M in THF, 0.13 mL, 0.13
mmol) was added dropwise to a solution of sulfone 8 (85 mg, 0.11 mmol) in
THF (0.3 mL) at -60 °C, and stirred for 40 minutes at this temperature.
Aldehyde 32 (31 mg, 0.16 mmol) in DMF (0.9 mL) and HMPA (0.13 mL) was
cannulated to a solution of sulfone 10 at -78 °C. The yellow solution was
stirred for 1 hour at -78 °C and then warmed slowly to room temperature.
After 12 hours, the reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl (2
mL). The reaction mixture was transferred to a separatory funnel and
extracted with Et2O (3 × 5 mL). The combined organic extracts were washed
with brine (5 mL), dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated by rotary
evaporation to give 39 as a colorless oil that was purified by flash
chromatography (Hexanes:THF = 200:1 → 50:1) to afford 39. Colorless oil;
Yield: 48 mg (60 %, 83 % based upon recovered starting material, E:Z =
12:1). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.59 (dt, J= 15.3, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 5.27
(dd, J= 15.4, 8.3 Hz, 1H), 3.87 (m, 1H), 3.83 (dd, J= 9.6, 4.8 Hz, 1H),
3.66 (s, 3H), 3.64 (dd, J= 6.3, 3.0 Hz, 1H), δ 3.51 (dd, J= 14.1, 7.8 Hz,
1H), 3.41 (t, J= 9.3 Hz, 1H), 3.21 (s, 3H), 2.33 (m, 3H), 2.14 (m, 2H),
1.91 (m, 1H), 1.71 (dd, J= 11.8, 6.6 Hz, 1H), 1.52 (dd, J= 14.2, 7.1 Hz,
1H), 1.41 (m, 1H), 1.04 (m, 21H), 0.99 (m, 9H), 0.96 (t, J= 7.8, 9H),
0.87 (s, 9H), 0.61 (q, J= 7.5 Hz, 6H), 0.05 (s, 3H), 0.04 (s, 3H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.45, 132.63, 130.39, 80.53, 76.41, 72.68,
65.24, 55.78, 51.34, 42.54, 41.37, 39.79, 38.68, 30.30, 27.02, 26.03,
20.10, 18.04, 15.62, 11.94, 10.73, 7.07, 5.62, -3.88, -4.13; LRMS (ESI)
calculated for C39H82O6Si3 (M+Na) 753, found 753.
