$DATUM (E)-Ethyl 7-(benzyloxy)hept-2-enoate (19) 2 To a stirred solution of
Ph3P=CHCO2Et (3.2 g, 9.3 mmol) in benzene (10 mL), was added the aldehyde
11a (1.5 g, 7.8 mmol) in benzene (10 mL) at 90 °C. After 4h, the solvent
was removed under reduced pressure and the crude product was purified by
silica gel column chromatography using hexane-ethyl acetate (9:1) as
eluent to afford the title compound 19 (1.88 g, 83%) as a colorless
liquid; IR (KBr) ν 2934, 2859, 1721, 1621, 1454, 1364, 1267, 1168, 1104,
1042, 984, 738, 698 cm-1; 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.33-7.21 (m, 5H),
6.98-6.83 (m, 1H), 5.77 (d, J = 15.3 Hz, 1H), 4.45 (s, 2H), 4.15 (q, J =
7.3 Hz, 2H), 3.44 (t, J = 5.8 Hz, 2H), 2.26-2.16 (m, 2H), 1.66-1.54 (m,
4H), 1.28 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 166.2, 148.6,
138.2, 128.0, 127.3, 121.0, 72.6, 69.5, 59.7, 31.6, 28.9, 24.4, 14.0;
ESIMS (m/z): C16H23O3 [M+H]+: 263.3
