$DATUM Compound 49: To a solution of alcohol 48 (4.05 g, 18 mmol) in
dichloromethane (90 mL) cooled at 0 °C was added IBX (6 g, 21.6 mmol) in
DMSO (18 mL) and the reaction mixture stirred at room temperature for 8 h
when TLC examination revealed completion of the reaction. The reaction
mixture was then diluted with dichloromethane (40 mL) and the
precipitated solids were filtered through a pad of Celite. The filtrate
was successively washed with water (3x50 mL), brine and dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4. The organic phase was evaporated under reduced pressure
to afford a crude aldehyde, which was taken ahead to the next step
without further purification. Thus to the above aldehyde in benzene (90
mL) was added ethyl(triphenylphosphoranylidine)acetate (6.91 g, 19.8
mmol) and stirred at room temperature for 6 h. The solvent was evaporated
under reduced pressure, diethyl ether (100 mL) was added to the residue
and the reaction mixture was cooled at 0 °C. The precipitated solids were
filtered and the filtrate was evaporated to dryness. The residue was
purified by column chromatography using 5% EtOAc/hexane (v/v) as the
eluent to the afford ester 49 (4.37 g, 14.9 mmol) in 83% yield as a
viscous oil. TLC: Rf 0.4 (10% EtOAc/hexane). IR (neat): 2980, 2927, 1717,
1654, 1459, 1427, 1272, 1191, 994, 756, 725 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.82 (dd, J = 1.3, 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.71 (dd, J = 1.3, 8.1 Hz, 1H),
7.38 (dt, J = 1.3, 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.25 (dt, J = 1.3, 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.02-6.92
(m, 1H), 5.89 (td, J = 1.5, 15.7 Hz, 1H), 4.16 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 3.48
(t, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 2.81-2.73 (m, 2H), 1.28 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR
(50 MHz, CDCl3): δ 165.6, 165.5, 152.7, 145.0, 134.8, 125.6, 123.9,
122.8, 121.1, 120.6, 59.9, 31.5, 31.1, 13.9. MS (ESI): 294 [M+H]+. HRMS
(ESI): m/z [M+Na]+ calcd for C14H15NO2NaS2 316.0441, found 316.0437.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
