$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Gratifyingly, Julia-Kocienski olefination between sulfone 24 and the
aldehyde 26 in the presence of LHMDS proceeded smoothly to provide 22 in
83% yield. Rf = 0.28 (2% EtOAc in hexane); [α]D 20 -27.6 (c0.50, CHCl3 ).
IR (neat): 3020, 2931, 1657, 1216, 1045, 669 cm-1 . 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3 ): δ = 5.45-5.42 (2 H, m), 4.09-4.05 (3 H, m), 3.80-3.74 (1 H, m),
3.66 (1 H, dd, J= 11.3, 4.8 Hz), 2.13-2.03 (4 H, m), 1.63-1.53 (2 H, m),
1.40 (3 H, s), 1.31 (3 H, s), 1.10 (3 H, d, J= 6.1 Hz), 0.90 (9 H, s),
0.88 (9 H, s), 0.86 (9 H, s), 0.11 (3 H, s), 0.08 (3 H, s), 0.06 (6 H,
s), 0.04 (3 H, s), 0.03 (3 H, s). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3 ): δ = 132.0,
127.2, 107.8, 77.4, 76.4, 72.6, 68.8, 65.3, 43.0, 30.1, 29.1, 28.4, 26.0,
25.96, 25.90, 23.3, 18.4, 18.1, -3.5, -4.5, -4.6, -4.7, -5.3, -5.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
