$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-diethyl non-2-en-1-ylphosphonate (6c). Sulfonylphosphonate 3 (476 mg,
1.27 mmol, 1 equiv.) was dissolved in THF (5.1 mL, 0.25 M) and cooled to
-78 °C. KHMDS (304 mg, 1.53 mmol, 1.2 equiv., 1 M in THF) was added
slowly. After five minutes at -78 °C, hexanal (0.23 mL, 1.91 mmol, 1.5
equiv.) was added to the solution. After 20 minutes, the reaction mixture
was warmed up to 0 °C. After 1 hour, the reaction was quenched by
addition of aqueous NH4Cl solution and the product was extracted with
EtOAc. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and
then concentrated in vacuo. The reaction mixture was purified by column
chromatography (grad. 15%→30% acetone in hexanes). (274 mg, 1.10 mmol,
87%, >95:5 E:Z by 1H NMR) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (500MHz, CDCl3) δ
5.60 (dt, J = 6.6, 15.2 Hz, 1H), 5.39 (dt, J = 7.3, 15.2 Hz, 1H), 4.09
(m, 4H), 2.54 (dd, J = 7.3, 21.5 Hz, 2H), 2.03 (q, J = 6.5 Hz, 2H),
1.40-1.22 (m, 12H), 0.88 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ
136.3 (d, J = 4.7 Hz), 118.4 (d, J = 11.3 Hz), 61.8 (d, J = 6.4 Hz), 32.5
(d, J = 2.5 Hz), 31.3, 30.5 (d, J = 139.9 Hz), 29.9, 28.8 (d, J = 3.4
Hz), 22.5, 16.4 (d, J = 5.9 Hz), 14.0; HRMS (ES) m/z calcd for C13H27O3P
[M+H]+ 249.1614, found 249.1614; IR (thin film, cm-1) 2980, 2958, 2928,
2858, 1458, 1444, 1392, 1368, 1254, 1215, 1164, 1098, 1054, 1030, 963,
835, 783, 708, 666.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective (E:Z=>95:5), Julia-Kocienski olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of conjugated polyenes via sequential condensation of
sulfonylphosphonates and aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cichowicz, Nathan R.; Nagorny, Pavel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(4), 1058-1061

