$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B: Preparation of
Trisubstituted Olefins To a flame-dried round bottom flask equipped with
a magnetic stir bar was added freshly prepared lithium diisopropyl amide
(LDA, 19.0 mg, 0.174 mmol) in dry THF. The solution was cooled to -78 °C.
Under the Barbier conditions,1 a solution in THF of 6h (26 mL, 0.237
mmol) and 5 (50.0 mg, 0.158 mmol) was added slowly to the LDA/THF
solution at -78 °C. The reaction was stirred overnight, approximately
15-18 hours while warming to room temperature, until the reaction deemed
complete by TLC analysis. The reaction was quenched on saturated ammonium
chloride solution in water, extracted with ethyl acetate (3x), washed
with brine, dried over magnesium sulfate, and concentrated in vacuo. The
resulting crude material was purified using silica gel chromatography
(ethyl acetate/pentane) to afford 4h. Compound 4c was prepared by General
Procedure B to afford a homogeneous clear oil in 82% yield and >95:5 Z
stereochemistry as evidenced by NOE and 1H NMR spectroscopy.
1H-NMR(CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 7.11-7.05 (m, 6H) 6.90-6.89 (d, 2H), 6.39 (s,
1H), 2.35 (s, 3H), 2.19 (s, 3H); 1H-NMR NOE (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 6.39 1H
<-> 2.18 3H (3.7%); 2.18 3H <-> 6.39 1H (7.9%); 13C-NMR(CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ
139.8, 138.8, 137.1, 136.5, 131.8, 130.4, 129.5, 128.2, 128.1, 125.2,
27.4, 21.5; IR (film cm-1) 3129, 1668, 1422, 1370, 1246, 1173, 1142,
1086, 1059, 809, 753, 670; Exact mass calcd for [M+H] requires m/z
242.0862 Found 242.0862 (ES+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Julia olefination, Barbier conditions, Z:E g.t. 95:5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Markovnikov-Selective Hydrothiolation of Styrenes: Application to the
Synthesis of Stereodefined Trisubstituted Olefins
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Savolainen, Markku A.; Wu, Jimmy
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(14), 3802-3804

