$DATUM (2R,4S,6R)-4-Methoxymethoxy-2,6-dimethyl-7-methylenenonan-1-ol (16) from
19. To a cooled (0 °C) mixture of methyltriphenylphosphonium bromide
(2.49 g, 6.98 mmol) in THF (15 mL) was treated with n-BuLi (2.8 mL, 6.7
mmol) in n-hexane (2.4 M), and the reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 30 min. To the reaction mixture was added a solution of
ketone 19 (853 mg, 2.33 mmol) in THF (4 mL) dropwise at 0 °C and the
reaction mixture was stirred for 10 min at room temperature. After being
stirred for 12 h at 40 °C, the reaction was quenched by addition of
saturated aq. NH4Cl (20 mL) and extracted with Et2O (3×50 mL). The
combined organic layer was washed with brine (20 mL), dried with Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated. A silica gel column chromatography
(n-hexane/Et2O 20:1→10:1) afforded PMB ether (688 mg, 81%) as a colorless
oil; [α]D 23 +19.1 (c 3.07, CHCl3); IR (neat) ν max 2959, 1613, 1514,
1458, 1248, 1096, 1039 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.25 (2H d, J =
8.6Hz), 6.87 (2H d, J = 8.6Hz), 4.74 (1H, m), 4.72 (1H, m), 4.65 (1H, d,
J = 6.9Hz), 4.59 (1H, d, J = 6.9Hz), 4.43 (2H, s), 3.80 (3H, s), 3.60
(1H, m), 3.37 (3H, s), 3.29 (1H, dd, J = 9.1, 5.7Hz), 3.20 (1H, dd, J =
9.1, 6.8Hz), 2.27 (1H, q, J = 7.0Hz), 2.01 (1H, m), 1.97 (1H, m), 1.93
(1H, m), 1.61 (1H, m), 1.57 (1H, m), 1.52 (1H, m), 1.23 (1H, m), 1.03
(3H, t, J = 7.5Hz), 1.01 (3H, d, J = 6.9Hz), 0.96 (3H, d, J = 6.6Hz) ;
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 158.96, 155.69, 130.76, 129.06, 113.63,
106.88, 95.69, 75.70, 74.52, 72.52, 55.62, 55.21, 41.31, 39.42, 36.93,
29.95, 25.84, 20.64, 17.35, 12.33; ESIMS (positive) m/z 387 (M+Na)+;
HRESIMS (pos.) m/z 387.2502[(M+Na)+, calcd for C22H36O4Na, 387.2506].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Wittig reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total Synthesis of Amphidinolide Q
