$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 16: To a stirred solution of sulfone 14 (11 mg, 22 mmol),
aldehyde 15 (13 mg, 26 mmol) and LiCl (4.0 mg, 78 mmol) in MeCN (1.0 mL)
at 0 °C, DBU (12 mL, 78 mmol) was added dropwise. After stirring for 20
min, the reaction mixture was quenched with sat. aq NH4Cl and extracted
with CH2Cl2. The organic layer was washed with sat. aq NH4Cl and brine,
dried over MgSO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
preparative TLC. 16 (11 mg, 18 mmol, 81%). Spectral data for 16: IR
(neat): 839, 1116, 1573, 1693, 2927 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
0.25 (s, 6 H), 1.02 (s, 9 H), 3.50 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 2 H), 5,04 (s, 2 H),
5.08 (s, 4 H), 6.25-6.27 (m, 2 H), 6.65 (d, J = 11.6 Hz, 1 H), 6.82 (s, 2
H), 6.91 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.10-7.43 (m, 17 H); 13C NMR (68 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = -4.1, 18.3, 25.8, 33.6, 71.1, 71.2, 75.3, 105.9, 118.4,
121.1, 127.2, 127.3, 127.4, 127.7, 127.8, 128.1, 128.4, 128.5, 128.6,
130.3, 130.5, 130.7, 133.5, 137.2, 137.8, 137.9, 152.9, 153.4; FABMS: m/z
= 642 [M]+; HRMS: m/z [M]+ calcd for C42H46O4Si: 642.3165; found:
642.3162.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, E/Z=27:1, Masamune-Roush condition, Julia-Kocienski
reaction
