$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of sulfone (1.8 g, 4.16 mmol) in dry THF (20 mL) at -78 °C was
treated with lithium bis(trimethyl)amide (4.98 mL, 1.0 M in THF, 4.98
mmol). The resultant red color solution was stirred at -78 °C for 30 min,
after which a solution of aldehyde 13 (1.0 g, 5.37 mmol) in dry THF (10
mL) was added slowly. The reaction mixture was stirred at -78 °C for 2 h
and allowed to warm to ambient temperature overnight. The cloudy reaction
mixture was quenched with water (2 mL) and poured into brine (30 mL). The
layers were separated and extracted with EtOAc. The combined extracts
were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo. Flash
chromatography (10% EtOAc-hexane). (1.4 g, 80%) as a pale yellow oil.
[α]25D -10.2 (c 1, CHCl3); IR (KBr): 2933, 2857, 1454, 1351, 1102, 1035
cm-1 ; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 5.45-5.26(m, 2H), 4.72 (t, 1H, J= 3.58
Hz), 3.80-3.68 (m, 1H), 3.66-3.58 (m, 1H), 3.46-3.3.34 (m, 2H), 3.23 (s,
3H) 3.08-2.97 (m, 1H) 2.17-1.92 (m, 4H), 1.82-1.69 (m, 2H) 1.66-1.42 (m,
8H), 1.36-1.22 (m, 10H), 0.89 (t, 3H, J= 6.4 Hz); 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 132.02, 126.49, 98.76, 80.98, 66.94, 62.20, 56.43, 36.30,
33.29, 31.79, 30.71, 29.71, 29.48, 29.26, 25.45, 25.22, 22.61, 19.58,
14.04; ESIMS m/z [M + Na]+: 349.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Julia-Kocienski olefination, slow addition of aldehyde
stage 2
