$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM ((3E,5E,7E)-8-cyclohexylocta-3,5,7-trien-1-yl)benzene (7a). Allylic
phosphonate 5a (257 mg, 0.83 mmol, 1 equiv.) was dissolved in THF (3.3
mL, 0.25 M) and cooled to -78 °C. nBuLi (0.35 mL, 0.91 mmol, 1.1 equiv.,
2.5 M in hexanes) was added slowly. After 20 minutes at -78 °C,
cyclohexanecarbaldehyde (0.15 mL, 1.25 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) was added to the
solution. After 15 minutes, the reaction mixture was warmed up to rt and
allowed to stir for 12 hours. The reaction was then quenched by addition
of aqueous NH4Cl solution and the product was extracted with EtOAc. The
organic layer was washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and then
concentrated in vacuo. The reaction mixture was purified by column
chromatography (grad. 0%→2% EtOAc in hexanes). (185 mg, 0.70 mmol, 83%,
90:10 EEE:Σ(other) by 1H NMR) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (700MHz, CDCl3)
δ 7.30-7.24 (m, 2H), 7.22-7.15 (m, 3H), 6.11-6.05 (m, 3H), 6.01 (dd, J =
8.9, 15.2 Hz, 1H), 5.68 (dt, J = 7.0, 14.0 Hz, 1H), 5.63 (dd, J = 6.9,
15.1 Hz, 1H), 2.71 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 2.42 (q, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 2.01
(m, 1H), 1.78-1.70 (m, 4H), 1.68-1.61 (m, 1H), 1.32-1.05 (m, 5H), 1.09
(m, 2H); 13C NMR (175 MHz, CDCl3) δ 141.8, 140.6, 133.0, 131.6, 131.0,
130.7, 128.4, 128.3, 127.8, 125.8, 40.9, 35.8, 34.6, 32.8, 26.1, 26.0;
HRMS (EI) m/z calcd for C20H26 [M]+ 266.2034, found 266.2039; IR (thin
film, cm-1) 3085, 3062, 3015, 2924, 2851,1496, 1449, 1030, 994, 966, 754,
698.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (E:other=90:10), alternative preparation shown (use of
KHMDS or NaHMDS as a base gave lower yields), Horner-Wadsworth-Emmons
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of conjugated polyenes via sequential condensation of
sulfonylphosphonates and aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cichowicz, Nathan R.; Nagorny, Pavel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(4), 1058-1061

