$DATUM (2R,4S,6R)-4-Methoxymethoxy-2,6-dimethyl-7-methylenenonan-1-ol (16). To a
cooled (0 °C) mixture of methyltriphenylphosphonium bromide (3 g, 8.4
mmol) in THF (20 mL) was treated with n-BuLi (2.7 mL, 6.5 mmol) in
n-hexane (2.4 M), and the reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 30 min. To the reaction mixture was added a solution of
ketone 15 (1.13 g, 2.8 mmol) in THF (5 mL) dropwise at 0 °C and stirred
for 10 min at room temperature. After being stirred for 7 h at 40 °C, the
reaction was quenched by addition of saturated aq. NH4Cl (20 mL) and
extracted with Et2O (3×50 mL). The combined organic layer was washed with
brine (20 mL), dried with Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated. A silica
gel column chromatography (nhexane/ CHCl3 8:1 → 5:1, n-hexane/EtOAc 30:1)
afforded TIPS ether (883 mg, 79%) as a colorless oil: [α]D 23 +20.7 (c
2.83, CHCl3); IR (neat) ν max 2943, 2867, 1459, 1099, 1042 cm-1; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.75 (1H, m), 4.73 (1H, m), 4.65 (1H, d, J = 6.8Hz),
4.60 (1H, d, J = 6.8Hz), 3.59 (1H, m), 3.53 (1H, dd, J = 9.5, 5.4Hz),
3.45 (1H, dd, J = 9.5, 6.5Hz), 3.37 (3H, s), 2.29 (1H, m), 1.99 (1H, m),
1.80 (1H, m), 1.63 (1H, m), 1.57 (1H, m), 1.50 (1H, m), 1.23 (1H, ddd, J
= 14.1, 8.7, 4.6Hz), 1.06-1.03 (27H, m), 0.94 (3H, d, J = 6.6Hz) ; 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 155.74, 106.87, 95.66, 74.71, 68.73, 55.60, 41.45,
38.84, 36.92, 32.47, 25.93, 20.70, 18.04, 17.00, 12.32, 11.96; ESIMS
(positive) m/z 423 (M+Na)+; HRESIMS (pos.) m/z 423.3265 [(M+Na)+, calcd
for C23H48O3NaSi, 423.3265].
