$DATUM (E)-diethyl (3-cyclohexylallyl)phosphonate (6e). Sulfonylphosphonate 3
(1.05 g, 2.80 mmol, 1 equiv.) was dissolved in THF (11.2 mL, 0.25 M) and
cooled to -78 °C. KHMDS (671 mg, 3.37 mmol, 1.2 equiv., 1 M in THF) was
added slowly. After five minutes at -78 °C, cyclohexanecarbaldehyde (0.51
mL, 4.21 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) was added to the solution. After 20 minutes,
the reaction mixture was warmed up to 0 °C. After 1 hour, the reaction
was quenched by addition of aqueous NH4Cl solution and the product was
extracted with EtOAc. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried over
MgSO4, and then concentrated in vacuo. The reaction mixture was purified
by column chromatography (grad. 15%→30% acetone in hexanes). (577 mg,
2.20 mmol, 79%, >95:5 E:Z by 1H NMR) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (500MHz,
CDCl3) δ 5.55 (ddd, J = 6.2, 6.2, 15.4 Hz, 1H), 5.36 (dt, J = 6.5, 15.1
Hz, 1H), 4.09 (m, 4H), 2.54 (dd, J = 7.3, 21.4 Hz, 2H), 2.01-1.92 (m,
1H), 1.74-1.67 (m, 4H), 1.67-1.60 (m, 1H), 1.33-1.01 (m, 11H); 13C NMR
(125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 142.0 (d, J = 14.4 Hz), 116.0 (d, J = 11.0 Hz), 61.8
(d, J = 6.2 Hz), 40.8, 32.8 (d, J = 2.9 Hz), 30.6 (d, J = 139.5 Hz),
26.1, 26.0, 16.5 (d, J = 6.2 Hz); HRMS (ES) m/z calcd for C13H25O3P
[M+H]+ 261.1614, found 261.1615; IR (thin film, cm-1) 2980, 2952, 2852,
1478, 1448, 1392, 1367, 1253, 1164, 1098, 1059, 1029, 965, 893, 858, 832,
781, 712.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective (E:Z=>95:5), Julia-Kocienski olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of conjugated polyenes via sequential condensation of
sulfonylphosphonates and aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cichowicz, Nathan R.; Nagorny, Pavel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(4), 1058-1061

